+## scaleway_sd_configs
+
+Scaleway SD configuration{{% available_from "v1.151.0" %}} discovers scrape targets from [Scaleway](https://www.scaleway.com/en/) Instances.
+
+Configuration example:
+
+```yaml
+scrape_configs:
+- job_name: scaleway
+  scaleway_sd_configs:
+
+    # secret_key is used for authenticating requests to the Scaleway API via the X-Auth-Token HTTP header (mandatory).
+    # See: https://www.scaleway.com/en/docs/identity-and-access-management/iam/how-to/create-api-keys/
+  - secret_key: "..."
+
+    # project_id is the id of the project to discover instances from.
+    # Either project_id or organization_id must be set.
+    #
+    # project_id: "..."
+
+    # organization_id is the id of the organization to discover instances from.
+    # Either project_id or organization_id must be set.
+    #
+    # organization_id: "..."
+
+    # zone is the Scaleway availability zone to discover instances in.
+    # See https://www.scaleway.com/en/docs/console/account/reference-content/products-availability/
+    #
+    # zone: "fr-par-1"
+
+    # Scaleway provides query arguments to filter instances.
+    # See: https://www.scaleway.com/en/developers/api/instance/#path-instances-list-instances
+
+    # name_filter is an optional query argument to filter instances by name.
+    #
+    # name_filter: "..."
+
+    # tags_filter is an optional query argument to filter instances - only instances having all of the given tags are returned.
+    #
+    # tags_filter: ["...", "..."]
+
+    # port is an optional port to scrape metrics from.
+    # By default, port 80 is used.
+    #
+    # port: ...
+
+    # Additional HTTP API client options can be specified here.
+    # See https://docs.victoriametrics.com/victoriametrics/sd_configs/#http-api-client-options
+```
+
+Each discovered target has an [`__address__`](https://docs.victoriametrics.com/victoriametrics/relabeling/#how-to-modify-scrape-urls-in-targets) label set
+to `<IP>:<port>`, where `<IP>` is the discovered instance's public IPv4 address if it has one, otherwise its private IPv4 address, and `<port>` is the port from the `scaleway_sd_configs` (default port is `80`).
+
+The following meta labels are available on discovered targets during [relabeling](https://docs.victoriametrics.com/victoriametrics/relabeling/):
+
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_id`: the ID of the instance.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_name`: the name of the instance.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_hostname`: the hostname of the instance.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_arch`: the architecture of the instance, such as `x86_64` or `arm64`.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_boot_type`: the boot type of the instance.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_commercial_type`: the commercial type (instance type) of the instance, such as `DEV1-S`.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_organization_id`: the id of the organization the instance belongs to.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_project_id`: the id of the project the instance belongs to.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_public_ipv4`: the public IPv4 address of the instance, if it has one.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_private_ipv4`: the private IPv4 address of the instance, if it has one.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_state`: the state of the instance, such as `running`, `stopped` or `stopped in place`.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_zone`: the availability zone of the instance.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_tags`: comma-separated list of tags applied to the instance.
+
+Instances aren't filtered by state, so it is recommended to keep only the `running` instances via [`relabel_configs`](https://docs.victoriametrics.com/victoriametrics/relabeling/), for example:
+
+```yaml
+relabel_configs:
+- source_labels: [__meta_scaleway_instance_state]
+  regex: running
+  action: keep
+```
+
+The list of discovered Scaleway targets is refreshed at the interval, which can be configured via `-promscrape.scalewaySDCheckInterval` command-line flag, default: 30s.
+
 ## static_configs
 
 A static config allows specifying a list of targets and a common label set for them.
